src/models/cmp/data/raw/
src/mcp_server/data/prior_reads.jsonl

# ── runtime artifacts teammates need ──────────────────────────────────────────
# The blanket `data/` and `checkpoints/` rules above hid the trained models AND
# the preprocessing artifacts that go with them, so a fresh clone silently fell
# back to stubs — the tabular checkpoint was committed but its scaler and medians
# were not, and _load_artifacts() cannot run without both.
#
# These paths are FORCE-TRACKED (`git add -f`) rather than un-ignored with `!`:
# a negation cannot rescue a file whose parent directory is excluded, because git
# never descends into an excluded directory. Once tracked, these rules no longer
# apply to them.
#
#   src/models/vision/checkpoints/best_model.pt      3.1 MB
#   src/models/vision/data/class_map.json
#   src/models/tabular/data/{scaler,medians}.pkl
#   src/models/tabular/data/{feature_names.json,fail_profile.npy}
#   src/models/cmp/checkpoints/cmp_model.pkl         1.4 MB
#   src/models/cmp/data/{cmp_train.csv,feature_names.json}   1.9 MB
#   src/mcp_server/data/wafer_maps/*.npy             144 KB
#
# ~6.6 MB total. Training INPUTS stay ignored: X_train.npy is 868 MB,
# LSWMD.pkl 2.1 GB, and the raw CMP traces 189 MB. Regenerate those with
# data_prep.py.
